hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"19116","Sufyan ibn Uyayna narrated to us, from al-Zuhri, from Urwa, from Marwan and al-Miswar ibn Makhrama, one adding to the other: The Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) set out in the year of Hudaybiyya with ten-odd hundred of his companions, and when he was at Dhu al-Hulayfa he garlanded the sacrificial animals and marked them and entered ihram from there, and he sent a scout of his ahead of him, then the Messenger of Allah (peace and blessings of Allah be upon him) travelled until when [the source breaks off here]."
